{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794172765,"nonce":"oORj6D+l8XA/Hr3++SQGtITaZao=","title":"L2 — Workspace config and git-bug repo discovery","message":"## Context\nThe user adds single project dirs or parent dirs to scan; the app must find git repos that use git-bug.\n\n## Files\n- `src/workspace.rs` — new, exported from `src/lib.rs`\n\n## Approach\n- `cargo add directories`, `cargo add --dev tempfile`.\n- `Workspace { roots: Vec\u003cRoot\u003e, scan_depth: u8 /* default 4 */, dark: bool }`, `Root { path, kind: Project | Scan }`, serde JSON at `ProjectDirs::from(\"dev\", \"arkye03\", \"gbtracker\")` config dir `/workspace.json`. Missing file → default. Save via temp file + rename.\n- `discover(\u0026Workspace) -\u003e Vec\u003cRepoInfo { root, name, has_git_bug }\u003e`: `Project` → that dir; `Scan` → walk to `scan_depth`; a dir with `.git` (dir or file) is a repo and is not descended into; skip hidden dirs, `node_modules`, `target`; never follow symlinks.\n- Dedupe by git common dir (`git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir`): git-bug state lives there, shared by linked worktrees (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/lib/gb_core.sh:11-18`).\n- git-bug presence: `git for-each-ref --count=1 refs/bugs refs/identities` non-empty — cheap, takes no git-bug lock.\n\n## Depends on\nL1 — `src/lib.rs`\n\n## Out of scope\n- UI, issue loading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Tempdir tests: scan finds nested repos up to depth, skips `node_modules` and hidden dirs, stops at repo boundaries, dedupes a linked worktree, and flags git-bug presence after `git update-ref refs/bugs/x HEAD`\n- Save/load round-trip test against a temp config path\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}